<title>USA: Clinton budget to extend hardrock mining fees.</title>
<headline>Clinton budget to extend hardrock mining fees.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fees on hardrock mining set in 1993 would be extended to 1998 and beyond under the Clinton administration's fiscal 1998 budget plan released Thursday.</p>
<p>The proposal would extend the $100 claim maintenance fee and the $25 location fee. The fees would continue to be adjusted annually based on the Consumer Price Index.</p>
<p>The administration also said it would propose legislation to charge a five percent royalty on the net-smelter return from the production of hard-rock minerals produced on federal lands.</p>
<p>The royalties would be deposited in a new reclamation fund for the environmental restoration of abandoned mine sites on federal lands, the budget plan said.</p>
</text>
